{
  "$comment": "Cover styles (D-017). A style sets typography, layout, a motif and a few palette families, so every book can look different while staying right for its genre. Fonts are SIL OFL 1.1 families installed for the prototype (assets/fonts/README.md). Positions and sizes are in cover-width units (1 = 1% of the cover width; a 2:3 cover is 150 units tall). A book picks a style and a palette and may override title lines, sizes and the motif. Typographic covers are the free default; image covers come from the cover stage. Text stays inside the safe zone in paperback.cover.safeZone (unverified) and away from the barcode area (paperback.cover.barcodeArea, unverified).",
  "version": 1,
  "updatedOn": "2026-10-04",
  "units": "cover-width percent",
  "kdpRuleIds": [
    "paperback.cover",
    "ebook.cover",
    "paperback.cover.safeZone",
